From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shupeng Xue <dspxue@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:45:56 +1100
Subject: [PATCH wireless-next 08/21] wifi: b43: let mac80211 restore the state
 after a controller restart

b43_chip_reset() re-initialises the core and then reloads the channel
configuration and the BSS info, but not the keys: the init clears the
key memory and dev->key[], and nothing puts the keys back. With
hardware crypto, b43_generate_txhdr() then fails every encrypted frame
with -ENOKEY. The interface stays associated but no data gets through
until the connection is torn down and set up again by hand.

Drivers that lose their state on a reset ask mac80211 to replay it
with ieee80211_restart_hw(). Do that when the core was running: take
it down as before, mark the interface removed (mac80211 adds it
again), and let b43_op_start() bring the core up. The configuration
and BSS reloads become unnecessary there. A core that was only
initialised is re-initialised as before.

Tested on a BCM4331 at 2.4 GHz with WPA2 and the default hardware
crypto, restarting the controller three times through debugfs while
pinging the AP once a second. Before: still associated, but no echo
reply in the 30 s after any of the restarts. After: replies from the
first or second ping on, 26-28 of 30 answered.

Fixes: e4d6b7951812 ("[B43]: add mac80211-based driver for modern BCM43xx devices")
Assisted-by: pi:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c | 29 +++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
index 3eabe7b41add..b2876eb84dad 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -5244,19 +5244,24 @@ static void b43_chip_reset(struct work_struct *work)
 	if (prev_status >= B43_STAT_INITIALIZED)
 		b43_wireless_core_exit(dev);
 
-	/* ...and up again. */
-	if (prev_status >= B43_STAT_INITIALIZED) {
-		err = b43_wireless_core_init(dev);
-		if (err)
-			goto out;
-	}
+	/* Running: let mac80211 start us again and replay the whole
+	 * configuration. Reloading only the config and BSS info here left
+	 * the key memory, which the init clears, empty, so with hardware
+	 * crypto every frame was dropped for want of its key. mac80211 adds
+	 * the interface again, so it must look removed.
+	 */
 	if (prev_status >= B43_STAT_STARTED) {
-		err = b43_wireless_core_start(dev);
-		if (err) {
-			b43_wireless_core_exit(dev);
-			goto out;
-		}
+		wl->operating = false;
+		wl->vif = NULL;
+		mutex_unlock(&wl->mutex);
+		ieee80211_restart_hw(wl->hw);
+		b43info(wl, "Controller restart handed to mac80211\n");
+		return;
 	}
+
+	/* ...and up again. */
+	if (prev_status >= B43_STAT_INITIALIZED)
+		err = b43_wireless_core_init(dev);
 out:
 	if (err)
 		wl->current_dev = NULL; /* Failed to init the dev. */
@@ -5269,8 +5274,6 @@ static void b43_chip_reset(struct work_struct *work)
 
 	/* reload configuration */
 	b43_op_config(wl->hw, -1, ~0);
-	if (wl->vif)
-		b43_op_bss_info_changed(wl->hw, wl->vif, &wl->vif->bss_conf, ~0);
 
 	b43info(wl, "Controller restarted\n");
 }
